body:
Added requirement (reporter, 2026-11-23: "setup the various different providers api keys and do some automated tests before a user (me) gets involved"):

**Live provider smoke tests, run before the reporter's hand-test.** Add `#[ignore]` tests (lane: `live-ai`) that run only when a provider's key is in the environment (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) or when a local Ollama answers. Without a key, each test skips with a clear message, never fails. For each provider the test checks:
1. key lookup (environment, then keychain);
2. the status line reaches "Ready";
3. one short chat turn returns text;
4. one tool call (`get_job`) on a small fixture project succeeds;
5. a wrong key gives the "key rejected" status, not a crash.

Use the cheapest model of each provider. The key value must never appear in test output or logs. A maintainer's runner injects the keys into the test process environment only. The same lane serves #3782 (defaults) and #3783 (model list, custom endpoint / OpenRouter).
